Here is the commit message:
Check if player is in arena on food level change.

This commit fixes a bug.

During a food level change event, if the arena is running and the food level lock is enabled, we just need to also make sure that the given player is actually in the arena, otherwise it affects everyone on the server.

Here is the root cause:
The food level change event handler only checked whether the arena was running and whether `lockFoodLevel` was enabled before cancelling the event, without verifying that the specific player triggering the event was actually a participant inside the arena. Since this listener presumably listens to server-wide `FoodLevelChangeEvent`s (affecting all players on the server, not just arena participants), the missing player-scope check caused the food level lock to be incorrectly applied globally—any player on the server, even those not in the arena, had their food level changes cancelled whenever an arena instance was running with the lock enabled. The fix adds the missing `arena.inArena(p)` check to properly scope the cancellation logic to only affect players actually participating in the running arena.

Here is the patch:

     public void onFoodLevelChange(FoodLevelChangeEvent event) {
         if (!(event.getEntity() instanceof Player)) {
             return;
         }

         Player p = (Player) event.getEntity();

         if (arena.isRunning()) {
-            if (lockFoodLevel) {
+            if (arena.inArena(p) && lockFoodLevel) {
                 event.setCancelled(true);
             }
         } else {
             // Always locked in lobby/spec
             if (arena.inLobby(p) || arena.inSpec(p)) {
                 event.setCancelled(true);
             }
         }
     }



